course: dictionary
lesson: 9299
title: Specialise: becoming an expert
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To specialise means to focus on one subject or skill and work at it most of the time, until you become an expert. «To specialise is to focus on what you are best at» tells you the meaning straight away.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Keepers usually study animal care or biology and start as volunteers or trainees, and many specialise in birds, reptiles or big mammals.» Birds, reptiles and mammals are all kinds of animal, so specialise must mean to pick one kind and focus on it.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. Does "many keepers focus on birds" still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: To specialise means to study or work mainly on one subject or skill.
fact: «Specialise» is a verb, so it changes: specialises, specialised, specialising.
fact: «Specialise in» is a useful phrase: «She specialises in heart surgery.»
fact: A shop that specialises in something mainly sells that one thing, such as shoes or comics.
fact: In science, cells specialise: nerve cells and muscle cells become special types to do one job.
exercise: «She specialises in heart surgery.» What does specialises mean here? | *She works mainly on one kind of operation and becomes an expert in it | She spends her time learning to swim | She is very tired after lunch | She works in lots of different jobs every day
exercise: A shop that specialises in comics mostly sells what? | *Comics | Shoes | Bananas | Garden tools
exercise: «Hot countries grow bananas, while cooler countries make other things.» What does this show about specialise? | Cooler countries never make anything | Every country grows exactly the same food | *Each place focuses on what it is best at | Bananas are only grown in cold places
test: Which word fits the gap? A vet might ___ in horses. | Shout | *Specialise | Hop | Sneeze
test: Which word means to focus on one subject and become an expert in it? | Giggle | Wander | Remember | *Specialise
exam: Sam wants to work only on bones and become the best in the country. Which word describes his plan? | Wander | *Specialise | Giggle | Remember
